ir quality of life.", "FRIED:Fried is a prominent figure in the field of gerontology, recognized for co-authoring the recent consensus on frailty published in 2013. This work significantly contributed to the understanding of physical frailty in the elderly population. Additionally, Fried refers to a set of diagnostic criteria for frailty that was developed by a researcher in this area, further establishing its importance in assessing and addressing frailty among older adults.", "ROCKWOOD:Rockwood is a classification system designed to evaluate the physical capacity and fragility of elderly individuals. It categorizes these individuals based on their physical condition and levels of dependency, providing a structured approach to understanding their health status. Additionally, Rockwood is recognized as a co-author of the recent consensus on frailty published in 2013, which has significantly contributed to the understanding of physical frailty in the elderly population.", "SIX SOCIEDADES CIENTÍFICAS INTERNACIONALES:A collaboration of six international scientific societies that participated in the recent consensus on frailty.", "SÍNDROME DE FRAGILIDAD:The Síndrome de Fragilidad, or frailty syndrome, is a clinical condition primarily affecting the elderly, characterized by a notable decrease in functionality and an increased vulnerability to adverse health events. This syndrome manifests through a specific group of signs and symptoms that indicate an abnormality in the health and functional independence of older adults. Importantly, the frailty syndrome is treatable and reversible, highlighting the potential for intervention before significant functional deterioration occurs.", "DEPENDENCIA FUNCIONAL:Functional dependence refers to the inability to perform basic daily activities independently, often associated with frailty in the elderly.", "DISCAPACIDAD:DISCAPACIDAD refers to a condition characterized by reduced physical capabilities, which can arise from various factors, including sarcopenia. Additionally, disability is often a severe consequence of the frailty syndrome, highlighting the necessity for assistance in daily activities. This underscores the impact of disability on individuals' ability to perform everyday tasks and the importance of support systems for those affected.", "FACTORES NUTRICIONALES:\"FACTORES NUTRICIONALES\" refers to the nutritional elements that significantly influence the fragility and overall health of elderly individuals. These factors are crucial in both the development and management of frailty among the aging population, highlighting their importance in promoting better health outcomes for seniors.", "CRITERIOS DE FRIED:Los criterios de Fried son un conjunto de parámetros utilizados para diagnosticar la fragilidad en ancianos.", "VALORACIÓN MULTIDIMENSIONAL DE ROCKWOOD:La valoración multidimensional de Rockwood es una herramienta para evaluar la fragilidad en personas mayores.", "ENSRUD:Ensrud es un investigador que propuso criterios diagnósticos para la fragilidad en ancianos.", "INFARTO AGUDO DE MIOCARDIO:El infarto agudo de miocardio es un evento estresante que puede desencadenar disfunción homeostática y fragilidad.", "INTERLEUCINA-6:La interleucina-6 es un biomarcador que se relaciona con el riesgo de fragilidad en personas mayores.", "FACTOR DE CRECIMIENTO INSULÍNICO (IGF-1):El IGF-1 es un factor hormonal cuya disminución se relaciona con la fragilidad en ancianos.", "TESTOSTERONA:Testosterona es una hormona esteroide que desempeña un papel crucial en el desarrollo y la salud masculina. Se produce principalmente en los testículos y es esencial para el desarrollo de características masculinas, así como para la producción de esperma. Además, la testosterona influye en la regulación de la secreción de gonadotropinas en la adenohipófisis. En mujeres, la testosterona se produce principalmente en los ovarios y es clave en el desarrollo del hirsutismo, especialmente en aquellas con síndrome de ovario poliquístico.\n\nLa baja de testosterona se ha relacionado con la disminución de la fuerza física en ancianos, y su suplementación en hombres con hipogonadismo puede resultar en una disminución de la masa grasa y un aumento de la masa muscular y la fuerza. También se utiliza en el tratamiento del hipogonadismo para inducir y mantener la virilización y la función sexual normal. En resumen, la testosterona es fundamental tanto para el desarrollo de los tejidos reproductivos masculinos como para la promoción de características sexuales secundarias, influyendo significativamente en la salud y el bienestar general de los hombres."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}